{"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/s15BitwiseCopyableP","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/s12CaseIterableP","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/Se","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/SE","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/SQ","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/SH","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WritingDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Writing direction defines the base direction in which bidirectional text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lays out its directional runs. A directional run is a contiguous sequence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of characters that all have the same effective directionality, which can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be determined using the Unicode BiDi algorithm. The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/leftToRight","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writing direction puts the directional run that is placed first in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"storage leftmost, and places subsequent directional runs towards the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"right. The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/rightToLeft","type":"reference"},{"text":" writing direction puts the directional run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that is placed first in the storage rightmost, and places subsequent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"directional runs towards the left.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that writing direction is a property separate from a text’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alignment, its line layout direction, or its character direction."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"However, it is often used to determine the default alignment of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paragraph. E.g. English (a language with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale\/LanguageDirection\/leftToRight","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locale\/Language-swift.struct\/characterDirection"},{"type":"text","text":") is usually aligned"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the left, but may be centered or aligned to the right for special"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effect, or to be visually more appealing in a user interface."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For bidirectional text to be perceived as laid out correctly, make sure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that the writing direction is set to the value equivalent to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locale\/Language-swift.struct\/characterDirection"},{"text":" of the primary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"language in the text. E.g. an English sentence that contains some","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Arabic (a language with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale\/LanguageDirection\/rightToLeft","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locale\/Language-swift.struct\/characterDirection"},{"text":") words, should use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/leftToRight","type":"reference"},{"text":" writing direction. An Arabic sentence that contains","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"some English words, should use a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/rightToLeft","type":"reference"},{"text":" writing direction.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing direction is always orthogonoal to the line layout direction"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"chosen to display a certain text. The line layout direction is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"direction in which a sequence of lines is placed in. E.g. English text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is usually displayed with a line layout direction of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale\/LanguageDirection\/topToBottom","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". While languages do"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have an associated line language direction (see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locale\/Language-swift.struct\/lineLayoutDirection"},{"type":"text","text":"), not all displays"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of text follow the line layout direction of the text’s primary language."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Horizontal script is script with a line layout direction of either","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale\/LanguageDirection\/topToBottom","type":"reference"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale\/LanguageDirection\/bottomToTop","type":"reference"},{"text":". Vertical script","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale\/LanguageDirection\/leftToRight","type":"reference"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale\/LanguageDirection\/rightToLeft","type":"reference"},{"text":" line layout","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"direction. In vertical scripts, a writing direction of ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/leftToRight","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is interpreted as top-to-bottom and a writing direction of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/rightToLeft","type":"reference"},{"text":" is interpreted as bottom-to-top.","type":"text"}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Working-with-writing-directions","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/leftToRight","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/rightToLeft"],"title":"Working with writing directions"},{"anchor":"Encoding-and-decoding","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/init(from:)"],"title":"Encoding and decoding"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/Equatable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString"]]},"metadata":{"platforms":[{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"26.0"},{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"26.0"},{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"26.0"},{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"26.0"},{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"tvOS","introducedAt":"26.0"},{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"visionOS","introducedAt":"26.0"},{"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"watchOS","introducedAt":"26.0"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WritingDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","title":"AttributedString.WritingDirection","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WritingDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:20FoundationEssentials16AttributedStringV16WritingDirectionO","modules":[{"name":"FoundationEssentials"}],"extendedModule":"FoundationEssentials","symbolKind":"enum"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The writing direction of a piece of text."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Supporting-types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/AttributeInvalid